{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '961,992p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1305,1314p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '90,114p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc; sed -n '1228,1246p' test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_world.cljc; sed -n '134,205p' test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_scenarios.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn decode\n  \"Validate and expand a row pack, including canonical cursor-cell numbering.\n   For task roots, run X1 and frame validation after numbering.\"\n  ([wire] (decode* wire default-budget))\n  ([wire budget] (decode* wire (dissoc budget :check-numbering))))\n\n\n(defn canonical-under\n  \"Test-only §5.5 re-emission under an explicit stream correspondence.\n   Missing marker coverage fails; neither traversal order nor original\n   cursor-cell numbering chooses a logical identity. Accepts a carrier.\"\n  [wire correspondence]\n  (let [task (decode* wire (assoc default-budget :check-numbering false))]\n    (letfn [(rewrite-slot\n              [d x]\n              (cond (ref? d) (rewrite x) (refs? d) (mapv rewrite x)\n                    (and (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d) (= :row (first x))) [:row (rewrite (second x))]\n                    :else x))\n            (rewrite\n              [n]\n              (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n                (if (= :stream kind)\n                  (let [id (first slots)]\n                    (when-not (contains? correspondence id) (bad! :missing-stream-correspondence [id]))\n                    (node :stream [(get correspondence id) (get correspondence id)]))\n                  (node kind (mapv rewrite-slot (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n      (emit (rewrite task)))))\n\n\n(defn- value-node\n  [x]\n  (check-literal-markers! x)\n(defn pack-address\n  \"The storage identity of a carrier: the BLAKE3 segment address of its\n   canonical bytes, distinct from the semantic root id it carries (§3.3).\"\n  [wire]\n  (jing/segment-key wire))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Task transport (continuation design §7): lift-task and lower-task\n;; =============================================================================\n      (when-not (and (cbor/byte-payload? bytes) (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: hash-mismatch\"\n                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch\n                         :yin.k/address address\n                         :yin.k/computed (computed-address address bytes)})))\n      (let [wire (try (cbor/decode bytes)\n                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: undecodable\"\n                                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path []\n                                         :yin.k/kind :bytes :yin.k/refusal (cbor/refusal e)}))))]\n        (if (map? wire)\n          (inspect-pack wire)\n          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path [] :yin.k/kind :body})))))\n                    [(assoc w :other (:yin.k/target e)) {:other (->data (:yin.k/target e))}])\n    :snapshot (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n                ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key (first args) :snapshot snap})\n                [w {:snapshots {(first args) snap}}])\n    :binding (let [b (->data (holder-binding w (first args)))]\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :binding :holder (first args) :binding b})\n               [w {:bindings {(first args) b}}])\n    :inject (let [[h request] args\n                  n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n              (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h]) request)\n              [(first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)) nil])\n    :offer-variant (let [[h] args\n                         v (offer-variant! w h)]\n                     ((:emit! ctx) {:event :variant :address (:addr